        "body": "## Apple Silicon support\n\nRun ESMFold2 binder design and the final critic on Apple Silicon through PyTorch/MPS. Download and extract the source archive below, then run the following from its top-level directory in a native arm64 terminal with Git and uv installed.\n\n```bash\n./install-macos.sh\nsource \"$HOME/esmfold2-mac/env.sh\"\nesmfold2-pipeline launch example_configs/apple/pdl1-vhh.yaml --esm-repo \"$ESM_REPO\"\n```\n\nFor optional Protenix V2 validation on Metal, add `--protenix-data /path/to/protenix-data` to the installer command. Supply the V2 checkpoint at `checkpoint/protenix-v2.pt` inside that directory. [Apple Silicon guide](https://github.com/cytokineking/esmfold2-pipeline/blob/v1.1.0/guide/apple-silicon.md)\n\n## Other changes since v1.0.1\n\n- Rank designs using ESMFold2 and validator confidence together with binder pose agreement after target alignment.\n- Score the binder–target interface using native Protenix expected-TM data and export validation diagnostics.\n- Preserve target sequences when resuming planned campaigns and use the prepared sequences for validation.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe 150-step PD-L1/VHH design and final critic completed in 22 min 22 s on a 128 GB M5 Max. On an NVIDIA A100 80 GB, the Linux installer built fresh CUDA 12.8 environments and a two-step design completed through template-enabled Protenix V2 validation and ranking. The CUDA suite passed all 411 tests. [Port verification](https://github.com/cytokineking/esmfold2-pipeline/pull/4)\n\nThe source archive includes both platform installers and the example inputs. The wheel contains the Python package. Verify either download against the attached SHA256SUMS.\n",
        "created_at": "2026-11-07T00:26:24Z",
